    <statement><p>Consider the shaded region in the graph below.</p>
<image xmlns:pi="http://pretextbook.org/2020/pretext/internal" pi:generated="webwork/images/Library__Michigan__Chap16Sec2__Q13__pg-image-1.png" width="41%"/>
<p>Write <m>\int_R f\,dA</m> on this region as an iterated integral:</p>
<p><m>\int_R f\,dA = \int_a^b\int_c^d f(x,y)\, d</m><fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0001"/>
<m>d</m><fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0002"/>,</p>
<p>where</p>
<p><m>a =</m> <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0003"/>,</p>
<p><m>b =</m> <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0004"/>,</p>
<p><m>c =</m> <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0005"/>, and</p>
<p><m>d =</m> <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0006"/>.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>y</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>x</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>6</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>3x</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>18</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>x = 0</m> and <m>x = 6</m> and between
the lines <m>y = 3x</m> and <m>y = 18</m>, and so the iterated integral is
<me>\int_0^{6} \int_{3x}^{18}\, f(x,y)\, dy\, dx.</me>
Alternatively, we could have set up the integral as follows:
<me>\int_0^{18} \int_{0}^{\frac{y}{3}} f(x,y)\, dx\, dy.</me>



</solution>
